Throwing non-missile weapons works fine to tell if they are
cursed.  Thrown non-missile weapons don't get any cut in
damage versus thrown missile weapons so the only
disadvantage is no possibility of multi-fire.

I don't recall trying to throw non-weapon items that might be
cursed.  Gems/rocks are never generated cursed except in
bones piles.

Though plenty of monsters have thrown potions at me it is
very rare for me to throw a potion at a monster.  Retroactively
learning a potion was cursed is only helpful if you have a
stack so that further reduces the usefulness.  Thinking back
on this I don't recall throwing healing at a pet.  Too often my
pet gets killed in a couple of hits - I have been playing
knights recently and I just lost my horse to the mine town
priest in one hit before I could get him to follow me out of
the shrine.


